// spec: STM-002
//
// compiled: no
//
// ⚠️ Opted out of the compiled half because the compiled back end does not have
// this defect -- it refuses the construct (C-12), which is what STM-002 now
// requires.  The recording here is the interpreted behaviour, the one at fault.
//
// STM-002 refuses a declaration as an unbraced branch body.  It is accepted,
// and the name ESCAPES into the enclosing scope -- so the WriteLn below finds
// X, and the same program with a false condition would not.

if True then var X := 1;

WriteLn (X);
